  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A transverse wave propagating on a stretched string of linear density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>kgm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is represented by the equation</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> in metres and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is in seconds. The tension in the string (in Newton) is</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn></math>",
